Hey Resul (or Mr. E.),

it's possible to use BATMAN under Linux, and Linux only. Mac OS,
Windows and BSD are currently not supported due to some routing
specialities only available under Linux. Maybe its not hard to port it
to the other OSs (we had BSD support in the past), but there is=20
currently no maintainer/tester. If you're intersted in porting and/or=20
maintaining, we'd be happy if you can contribute. :D

About OLSR-Switch: I guess you mean the Windows GUI Tool [1] and=20
not the Simulator [2]. There is no such GUI tool for BATMAN as far as i
know (please correct me if i'm wrong). The only GUI i know is the BATMAN
web interface by Ludger Schmudde, available here [3], which is currently
outdated.

regards,
	Simon

[1] http://wiki.freifunk.net/OLSR_mit_Windows (sorry, german)
[2] http://www.olsr.org/docs/README-Olsr-Switch.html
[3] http://freifunk.schmudde.com/

